From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: edk2-cix <edk2-cix@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 08:58:11 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Platform/CIX/Sky1: selectable PCIe 64-bit MMIO window for
 large BARs

Every Sky1 root bridge gets a fixed 16 GB above-4G window, aligned to
16 GB.  A Resizable BAR must be aligned to its own size, so a 16 GB BAR
can only sit at the window base and leaves no room for the device's
other BARs or the bridge window: GPUs with 16 GB of VRAM fail to resize
and 24 GB cards (32 GB BAR) cannot be placed at all.

Add PcieWindowLib, which grows the x8 root bridge window upward from its
fixed hardware base to 32, 64 or 128 GB.  The new setup option 'PCIe
64-bit Window' selects the layout; Auto (default) reads the Resizable
BAR capability of the device behind each root port and picks the
smallest layout with 512 MB to spare, never the experimental 128 GB.
The other root bridges keep their stock windows.

The same window is used by PciHostBridgeLib (MemAbove4G/PMemAbove4G),
published through new ACPI RAM variables for the PCI0-4 _CRS and the
PRC0-4 _INI, and written into the device tree ranges, so UEFI, ACPI and
DT boots agree.

From Neol00/edk2-cix-unlocked V2.5 (tested on the Radxa Orion O6).
